1
00:00:02,279 --> 00:00:04,735
Now that we learned about single path

2
00:00:04,943 --> 00:00:05,537
segments,

3
00:00:06,612 --> 00:00:09,325
we can also work on the update and delete

4
00:00:09,325 --> 00:00:11,877
function. And let's continue with deleting

5
00:00:11,909 --> 00:00:13,033
because that's a bit easier.

6
00:00:13,819 --> 00:00:16,339
As I mentioned, typically you use a POST

7
00:00:16,387 --> 00:00:18,683
request for deleting unless you're building

8
00:00:18,731 --> 00:00:21,058
a REST API, which we aren't doing here.

9
00:00:22,262 --> 00:00:24,573
So therefore, I'll register a new POST

10
00:00:24,573 --> 00:00:24,926
route.

11
00:00:25,536 --> 00:00:27,382
And now again, the question is, what should

12
00:00:27,382 --> 00:00:28,201
be the path here?

13
00:00:28,826 --> 00:00:31,310
And I would say for deleting something, we

14
00:00:31,390 --> 00:00:34,146
also need the ID of what should be deleted.

15
00:00:34,755 --> 00:00:37,174
So even though that's a POST request, we

16
00:00:37,174 --> 00:00:39,658
don't even need to transport any data in the

17
00:00:39,738 --> 00:00:40,667
request body.

18
00:00:41,196 --> 00:00:43,663
It just is a convention to use POST for

19
00:00:43,727 --> 00:00:45,634
deleting because we manipulate something on

20
00:00:45,666 --> 00:00:46,147
the server.

21
00:00:46,708 --> 00:00:48,999
But we won't even need the POST request body

22
00:00:49,351 --> 00:00:52,364
because we can again just encode the ID in

23
00:00:52,460 --> 00:00:53,309
the URL

24
00:00:53,902 --> 00:00:56,177
as we did it for getting a single element.

25
00:00:56,899 --> 00:00:59,256
So we can grab that code and do the same

26
00:00:59,352 --> 00:01:01,982
thing here for our delete post route.

27
00:01:02,640 --> 00:01:03,891
Now these 2 routes here,

28
00:01:04,644 --> 00:01:06,489
this GET route and the POST route, will be

29
00:01:06,505 --> 00:01:08,253
different even though they have the same

30
00:01:08,269 --> 00:01:11,236
path because they act on different HTTP

31
00:01:11,236 --> 00:01:11,685
methods.

32
00:01:12,358 --> 00:01:14,475
You couldn't have the same method and the

33
00:01:14,523 --> 00:01:16,832
same path, that would not work. You must

34
00:01:16,913 --> 00:01:19,783
only have one route per path method

35
00:01:19,879 --> 00:01:22,429
combination. But here we got the same path

36
00:01:22,783 --> 00:01:25,005
but different methods, and therefore these

37
00:01:25,118 --> 00:01:27,244
technically are different routes that will

38
00:01:27,292 --> 00:01:29,692
be executed for different kinds of incoming

39
00:01:29,788 --> 00:01:30,255
requests.

40
00:01:31,318 --> 00:01:32,558
And then here we have our good old

41
00:01:32,558 --> 00:01:34,636
middleware
